  "articleBody": "Embarking on a tiny home journey can feel like a lot to take on, with so many decisions from design to construction. It’s easy to get bogged down in the details before you even begin. A common mistake is trying to map out every single step on your own without a clear roadmap. Another pitfall is not defining your true needs and priorities early on, which can lead to costly changes later. Some folks also jump straight to construction ideas without fully exploring the design possibilities or understanding what's truly feasible for their budget and lifestyle. It’s important to avoid thinking of a tiny home as just a smaller version of a conventional house; it requires a unique design approach. Lastly, underestimating the time and effort involved in the planning phase can set you back. Our process at Zen Tiny Homes simplifies things by guiding you through property assessment, custom design, and the build, ensuring every decision is intentional and aligned with your vision. If you’re feeling swamped, remember, you don't have to navigate it alone.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-02"
